> **Engineer note:** follow the two project conventions — Pure Function Testing /
> Command Verification (`read .empress/agents/coding-guidelines.md`) for *what you
> verify*, and Ponytail (`read .empress/agents/coding-guidelines-ponytail.md`) for
> *what you build* (laziest solution that works, YAGNI ladder, stdlib-first;
> mark deliberate shortcuts `ponytail:` with a ceiling + upgrade path). For
> non-trivial work, write a minimal design doc (behavior + Command/interface spec)
> first, then tests, then implementation. If a requirement is ambiguous, mark it
> `[ASSUMPTION]` and add it to your handoff list instead of silently deciding (§10).